examples.question_text:
A student writes $\frac{1}{4}>\frac{1}{2}$ because $4>2$.
These bars represent equal-sized wholes. Shade one quarter of the first bar and one half of the second bar. Use them to correct the comparison and explain the mistake.
One quarter:
[tikz]% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"geometry","base":[],"semantic":[],"reference":"template quarter-question"}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes="1"/>}
\path[use as bounding box] (-0.6,-10.6) rectangle (20.6,0.6);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (5,0)--(5,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (10,0)--(10,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (15,0)--(15,-10);
\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (0,0) rectangle (20,-10);
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
One half:
[tikz]% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"geometry","base":[],"semantic":[],"reference":"template half-question"}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes="1"/>}
